  clock: 2  # 5cd7
  nonce: 5cd7  # 5cd7
  message: "From WI-binod-pulal-lazar-nakor-vakup-jorut-zodan-rubog (branch jgstern-agent/fix/binod, commit 1cc2667cbe, not merged). Two facts for this item; no fix folded in.\n\n1. The trap now reaches the `packet` subcommand too. WI-binod makes `shell_env_sites` import `hypergumbo_lang_mainstream.bash` (`_SHELL_STATE_NAMES`, `_HOST_DESCRIPTION_NAMES`) so the packet follows the analyzer's own classification. That import resolves through the same sys.path pin, so a packet A/B selected by PYTHONPATH renders with the script's tree's bash.py. If this item's fix prints the resolved module paths, print them for `packet` as well as `collect`.\n\n2. A second workaround, for the packet arm only: a copy of the script in a directory with no `packages/` sibling (I used `<scratch>/basearm/scripts/measure-taint-precision.py` from `git show origin/dev:...`) finds nothing to pin, so PYTHONPATH decides. Control that the arms differed: the baseline arm's cert-manager packet lists checkhash.sh:21 (`${BASH_SOURCE[0]}`), the subject arm's does not."  # 5cd7
