- op: discuss  # 4ab4
  at: '2026-10-03T06:41:59Z'  # 4ab4
  by: agent  # 4ab4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4ab4
  clock: 4  # 4ab4
  nonce: 4ab4  # 4ab4
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). Defect real; TRIGGER CONDITION was wrong; scope widened. Title updated.\n- scripts/measure-taint-precision.py:97-100 inserts its own tree's packages, guarded by `if str(_pkg) not in sys.path`. The main .venv's editable-install .pth files already put the main checkout's packages/*/src on sys.path (after PYTHONPATH), so the main-tree script under the main venv inserts NOTHING and PYTHONPATH decides.\n- Repro (fake hypergumbo_core on PYTHONPATH): main-tree script + .venv/bin/python resolves the fake (no trap); a copy of the script in a tree with its own packages/ (a worktree) resolves that copy's tree (trap fires); main-tree script + /usr/bin/python3 without the editable install resolves the main tree (trap fires). So the trap fires for a worktree/clone copy of the script (the valav case) or an interpreter without the editable install, not \"whenever invoked from the working tree\".\n- WORSE SIBLINGS: scripts/measure-narrowing-headroom.py:72 and scripts/measure-catalogue-exposure.py:68 insert core's src at position 0 UNGUARDED. Both resolved the main tree even with PYTHONPATH set to the fake, and they pin only hypergumbo-core, so a PYTHONPATH arm gets a mixed tree (core from the script's tree, language packages from elsewhere). The measure-*-ab.py scripts run both arms in one process and are unaffected.\n- RECORDS AUDIT (the 10-02 triage asked for it): no committed record is demonstrably affected. 0003 and INV-fubag's 08-21 A/B: deltas carry the change's signature (35 added / 0 removed; 29 removed / 6 kept), which identical arms cannot produce. 0013/0014/0015/0016/0021: arms checked out in place, no PYTHONPATH. 0029: console-script entry, the insertion never runs. mojaz_remeasure: single arm. valav first baseline: affected, already discarded (taint_base_INVALID_ran_subject_code/). rovun: used the workaround. \"0015 reuses it\" referred to 0003's delta-census question, not this mechanism.\n- The suggested fix (print the resolved module paths) fits all three scripts."  # 4ab4
